{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790343648,"nonce":"t4jQpLMXnPn6ViB2cXgpko9Q7sk=","message":"Two corrections to the description, from checking the Generic arm of the compute() lowering in ssa.rs.\n\nA body of any kernel kind other than a matched elementwise shape that has a `yield` directly in it does not call the dispatch: it takes the yield-stack path and returns the last yielded value, so `@kernel matmul` followed by `yield x` silently returns x. That is the same silent-wrong-result shape as the reduce bug and should become the same compile error.\n\nThe dispatch call is not only a link-time problem in principle: `zynml run` on a braced `compute(A, B) @kernel(matmul) @device(\"cuda:0\") @workgroup(16, 16) { for ... }` panics in the Cranelift JIT with \"can't resolve symbol $Zyntax$compute\".","files":null}]}